/* ============================================================================
 * COMPETITIVE (RFx) workflow model, the two-lane structure (rfx-lifecycle spec).
 * Selected for competitive projects (isCompRFx). The SOLE-source model above is
 * the sole-source path. Differences: sourcing is the ACTIVE competitive EVENT
 * (not "skipped"); the fan-out is PER-FINALIST provisional prep lanes, each step
 * conditional on an executed contract; the award stays conditional until signed,
 * and the executed event SPLITS into a per-winner post-award project.
 * ==========================================================================*/
// #75 (Marc): the competitive-RFx Workflow is the SOURCING event ONLY, a clean break. It ends at
// "Move to negotiations" and completes when awarded / abandoned / canceled. The post-sourcing prep
// (Legal/Cyber/WwTP/onboarding) + MSA negotiation live on the Deal tab / the follow-on post-RFx projects.
